      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "misogyny",
      "label": "Misogyny",
      "description": "A set of beliefs and attitudes that hold women to be inferior to men and that justify discrimination or oppression against women. The meme uses the juxtaposition of the man's confident pose with the derogatory text to create a humorous but demeaning portrayal of male inadequacy, which is a form of misogynistic humor that devalues women's autonomy and reinforces patriarchal norms.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_46b31617"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_39c86176",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "arranged_marriage_mockery",
      "label": "Arranged marriage mockery",
      "description": "A stereotype that portrays arranged marriages as inherently oppressive or degrading, often used to mock or belittle the cultural practices of certain communities. In the context of this meme, the reference to 'bride price' may be used to imply that the woman is 'buying' the man, which is a form of mockery that reduces the value of marriage to financial terms and reinforces patriarchal norms.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_46b31617"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
